I'm trying to get my new webpages indexed by google, it seems as though the last crawl didn't see the new pages, what are some reasons that might happen and the solution?

Google missing your new web pages typically stems from a breakdown in Discovery (it doesn't know the URLs exist), Access (it is actively blocked), or Priority/Budget (it prioritized other content).  
Onely

Common Causes & Solutions

Orphaned Pages (Discovery)

Cause: The new pages lack internal links from existing, already-indexed pages, making them invisible to crawlers.  
Sight AI

Fix: Add internal links to your new pages from high-traffic, relevant pages on your site.  
Sight AI

Robots.txt Block (Access)

Cause: A blanket or directory-specific rule in robots.txt is blocking Googlebot.  
Sight AI

Fix: Check [yourdomain.com/robots.txt](https://yourdomain.com/robots.txt) for Disallow: directives covering your new URL paths.

Accidental noindex Tag (Access)

Cause: A CMS setting or leftover code added <meta name="robots" content="noindex"> to the page HTML.  
Sight AI

Fix: Inspect the page source or response headers and remove the noindex instruction.  
Embarque.io

Missing or Stale XML Sitemap (Discovery)

Cause: Your sitemap doesn't automatically update to include new URLs, or hasn't been submitted.

Fix: Ensure dynamic sitemap generation and resubmit the sitemap URL in Google Search Console (GSC).  
Google Help

Server Performance or Errors (Priority)

Cause: Googlebot hit 5xx server errors, slow response times, or heavy JavaScript rendering bottlenecks during its last visit and backed off.

Fix: Review server logs and GSC Crawl Stats; optimize page performance.  
Google Help

Thin or Duplicate Content (Priority)

Cause: If marked as "Discovered – currently not indexed" or "Crawled – currently not indexed", Google saw the URL or content but deprioritized indexing due to low perceived value or canonicalization confusion.  
Embarque.io

Fix: Strengthen the content quality and ensure rel="canonical" points to the exact, preferred URL.  
Embarque.io

