2. How to Prevent Your "Thank You" Page from Being Indexed
Leaving a page out of sitemap.xml isn't enough on its own—Google might still discover and index it if someone links to it or shares the URL.

To keep it 100% hidden from search results while letting customers view it after submitting a form:

Step A: Add a noindex tag directly to the Thank You HTML page
Inside the <head> section of your Thank You page (e.g., thank-you.html), add:

HTML
<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
Step B: Block crawlers in robots.txt
In your [https://colonialtreecare.net/robots.txt](https://colonialtreecare.net/robots.txt) file, paste the following content:

Plaintext
User-agent: *
Allow: /

# Exclude thank you page from search engine crawlers
Disallow: /thank-you.html
Disallow: /thank-you

# Sitemap location declaration
Sitemap: https://colonialtreecare.net/sitemap.xml
(Replace /thank-you.html with your actual thank-you page URL path).

Checklist After Uploading
Trailing Slashes: Ensure whether your location URLs load as /chesapeake or /chesapeake/. The sitemap <loc> tags must match the exact version your site loads.

Submit to Google Search Console: Go to GSC > Sitemaps > Enter sitemap.xml and submit.

Inspect URL: Use the top bar in Search Console to inspect [https://colonialtreecare.net/chesapeake](https://colonialtreecare.net/chesapeake) and click Request Indexing.




